      Update tree-sitter grammars: ocaml
      
      Automated grammar update for **ocaml**.
      
      ### ocaml
      
      - OCaml target parsing now accepts raw identifiers such as \#type and Unicode identifiers in declarations and qualified references. Writing these spellings directly in rule patterns remains unsupported.
      - OCaml target parsing now supports effect-handler cases, retaining effect arguments, continuation bindings, guards, and handler bodies. Direct effect-handler syntax in rule patterns remains unsupported.
      - OCaml target parsing now supports labeled tuple expressions, binding and match patterns, and types, including shorthand and typed components. Direct labeled-tuple syntax in rule patterns remains unsupported.
      - OCaml target parsing now accepts local opens in types, including dotted module paths and applicative functor paths. Existing limitations in polymorphic-variant and package-type AST detail remain.
      - OCaml target parsing now accepts short dependent functor types such as (X : S) -> S. Detailed module-type matching and this syntax in rule patterns remain unsupported.
      - OCaml target parsing now accepts quoted strings whose Unicode delimiters use equivalent composed and decomposed spellings, preserving their literal contents.
      
      Pin: `4a885a61` → [`0cc270ff`](https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-ocaml/tree/0cc270ff90ca09c29d0f2f9dec69ddfef55a3eff) (**v0.24.2**)
      
      Parser and CST files are regenerated; vendored grammar sources are copied from the selected upstream revisions.
      
      Test plan:
      
      - Grammar corpus and standalone CST checks.
      - Full build and OSS + Pro regression validation.
      
